      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it expected that each version of this interface will have a register that is defined in the enum at the start of the file? If not, that might seem a bit awkward as that enum grows but some of the other versions don\u0027t keep up with it because they don\u0027t have to.\n\nI wonder if it might make more sense to define the offsets as structures with names, so something like\n\n```\n/* I\u0027m saying v1 is optional here since v2 doesn\u0027t exist, but just trying to make a point */\nstruct kvm_cpufreq_offsets[_v1] \u003d {\n        .cur_freq_reg \u003d 0x0,\n        .set_freq_reg \u003d 0x4,\n};\n```\n\nYou can keep the pointers to these offsets structures opaque and type cast in the functions that use them?",
      "revId": "ba35458c874bc0349c36b805a10200648e4b6738",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
