      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T21:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`devm_*` functions should be used for allocating resources that are tied to the lifetime of a device. This is so that the resources can automatically be freed in case of an error while the device probes or when the device is removed from the system.\n\nIn this case however, it seems that the data structures allocated here should be tied to the lifetime of the policy structure. The policy structure can be freed without removing the device, but this structure would still be allocated for no reason.\n\nI think it\u0027d be best to use `kzalloc()` here instead, and `kfree()` in `kvm_cpufreq_cpu_exit()` and at the end of this function in case of an error.",
      "revId": "ba35458c874bc0349c36b805a10200648e4b6738",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
